subproblems.statement:
Let a, b, c, d ∈ ℝ, H : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ and h, f, ψ₀ : ℝ → ℝ. Assume:
- H(p) = h(p.1) for almost every p ∈ (a, b) × (c, d);
- f(t) = 0 for every t ∉ (a, b);
- ψ₀(α) = 0 for every α ∉ (c, d);
- ∫_ℝ ψ₀ = 1.
Then ∫_{ℝ×ℝ} f(p.1)·ψ₀(p.2)·H(p) dp = ∫_ℝ f(t)·h(t) dt. These are Bochner integrals; no integrability hypotheses are needed.
